#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:99 kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:114
msgid "KMLDonkey Setup Wizard"
msgstr "KMLDonkey волшебник"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:102
msgid ""
"<h1>KMLDonkey Setup Wizard</h1><p>Making KMLDonkey work can be a daunting "
"task for the uninitiated. This wizard will guide you through the basic steps "
"needed to get you up and running.</p><p>If you understand how to set up and "
"administer an MLDonkey core and want to configure KMLDonkey yourself, you "
"can safely skip this wizard; otherwise, press the \"Next\" button below to "
"get started.</p><p><em>Read the text in the wizard carefully; everything in "
"it is important.</em></p><p><b>WARNING:</b> Running this wizard will "
"<em>erase</em> any previous core connections you may have configured. It "
"will not affect any previous MLDonkey cores you have installed.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:117
msgid ""
"<h1>Download MLDonkey</h1><p>The first thing you need to do is obtain an "
"MLDonkey core. This is the actual file sharing tool for which KMLDonkey acts "
"as a frontend.</p><p>Visit one of the web sites listed below (just click on "
"the links), and download a binary package suitable for your system; "
"alternatively, if your system's package manager provides an MLDonkey "
"package, you can install that instead, and note where the \"mlnet\" binary "
"is installed for later (usually in "
"<em>/usr/bin</em>).</p><ul>%1</ul><p>Extract the package somewhere "
"convenient, and press \"Next\". Do not worry about configuring or starting "
"what you downloaded; we will do that later.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:133
msgid "Download MLDonkey"
msgstr "Симни MLDoneky"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:138
msgid ""
"<h1>Set Up a Work Folder</h1><p>You need a work folder for your MLDonkey "
"core. This is where it stores its configuration data, temporary files and "
"finished downloads. You should place it on a disk partition with a lot of "
"free space.</p><p>NOTE: You can change the locations where it stores "
"temporary files and finished downloads later, if you like.</p><p>Select your "
"work folder here:</p>"
msgstr ""

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:146
msgid "Select Your Work Folder"
msgstr "Изберете ја вашата работна папка"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:148
msgid "Set Up a Work Folder"
msgstr "Подеси работна папка"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:154
msgid ""
"<h1>Locate Your Core</h1><p>Now, select the full path to your MLDonkey core, "
"which you (or your distribution) downloaded earlier, below. If the archive "
"you downloaded only contained one file, then this is the core, otherwise "
"look for the file called \"mlnet\".</p>"
msgstr ""

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:159
msgid "Locate Your MLDonkey Core"
msgstr "Лоцирај го MLDonkey јадрото"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:161
msgid "Locate Your Core"
msgstr "Лоцирајте го вашето јадро"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:167
msgid ""
"<h1>Launcher Settings</h1><p>Now, you need to decide when you want the core "
"to be running. The easiest way is to start the core whenever you launch "
"KMLDonkey, and shut it down when you close the application. You can also "
"elect to have it running continuously when you are logged into your KDE "
"session, regardless of whether KMLDonkey is running.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:174
msgid "Start the core when KMLDonkey starts"
msgstr "KMLDonket кога започнува, започни со јадрото"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:175
msgid "Start the core when you log into KDE"
msgstr "Кога влегувате во KDE започни со јадрото"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:177
#, fuzzy
msgid "Launcher Settings"
msgstr "Подесувања за стартовачот"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:182
msgid ""
"<h1>Name Your Core</h1><p>The last thing you need to do is assign a name to "
"your core. This is for your own use only; the default \"MLDonkey\" is quite "
"adequate, but you can choose anything you like.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:187
msgid ""
"_: default name for wizard-created core connection\n"
"MLDonkey"
msgstr "MLDonkey"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:190
msgid "Name Your Core"
msgstr "Именувајте го вашето јадро"

#: kmldonkey/setupwizard.cpp:194
msgid ""
"<h1>Configuration Complete</h1><p>We now know enough to set up a working "
"MLDonkey configuration. Press \"Finish\" below to get things "
"started.</p><p>Remember, your finished downloads go into the "
"<em>incoming</em> folder under your work folder.</p><p>Enjoy KMLDonkey!</p>"
msgstr ""

